course: dictionary
lesson: 2667
title: Diabetes: an illness with sugar in the blood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Diabetes is an illness. Your body turns the food you eat into sugar, called glucose, and sends it around in your blood. With diabetes, the body cannot control the amount of sugar in the blood properly. Read the words around the word: «If a friend with diabetes looks shaky, pale and confused, tell an adult at once.» Shaky, pale and confused are signs that something is wrong, so diabetes must be a serious health problem.
explain: The helper is insulin. Insulin lets sugar from food pass into the cells, where it gives the body energy. If the body does not make enough insulin, or cannot use it well, sugar stays in the blood when it should not. That is why people with diabetes must check their blood sugar and sometimes take insulin.
explain: Diabetes is not something you can always see. «Many disabilities are invisible, such as diabetes or a heart problem.» A classmate with diabetes may look just like you, so never guess how someone feels from how they look. Some people need a snack or a quick break from class, and that is normal and allowed.
fact: Diabetes is an illness in which the body cannot control the amount of sugar in the blood properly.
fact: There are two main kinds: type 1 diabetes often starts in childhood, and type 2 diabetes is more common in adults.
fact: Insulin is the body's helper that lets sugar from food get into the cells for energy.
fact: «Diabetes» is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say «have diabetes», not «a diabetes».
fact: If someone with diabetes seems shaky, sweaty, confused or very pale, tell an adult at once, because they may need sugar quickly.
exercise: «Many disabilities are invisible, such as diabetes or a heart problem.» What does invisible mean here? | *You cannot easily see it | It is very large | You can hear it from far away | It is made of glass
exercise: Ella says diabetes is when the body cannot control the amount of sugar in the blood. What is diabetes? | *An illness with blood sugar the body cannot control properly | A type of school sport | A kind of sweet food | A feeling of being very tired after lunch
exercise: «If a friend with diabetes looks shaky, pale and confused, tell an adult at once.» What should you do? | Wait an hour and see what happens | Ignore it, because they will be fine | Ask them to run around the playground | *Tell an adult at once
test: Which helper lets sugar from food get into the cells for energy? | Pancreas | Oxygen | Glucose | *Insulin
test: Which kind of diabetes often starts in childhood? | Type 2 diabetes | Autism | *Type 1 diabetes | A heart problem
exam: «Diabetes» is best described as: | A type of school subject | *An illness where the body cannot control blood sugar properly | A sort of food | A kind of sport
